WEBVTT

00:00:00.550 --> 00:00:02.335
Lesson 7.4.

00:00:02.335 --> 00:00:04.300
Whale & entity analysis.

00:00:04.300 --> 00:00:06.682
By the end of this lesson, you'll be able

00:00:06.682 --> 00:00:09.915
to use large-holder data without copying wallets blindly.

00:00:11.215 --> 00:00:12.505
Here's the plan.

00:00:12.505 --> 00:00:14.190
First, the key ideas.

00:00:14.190 --> 00:00:16.905
Then, a worked example, step by step.

00:00:16.905 --> 00:00:18.430
Then, your checklist.

00:00:18.430 --> 00:00:20.592
And finally, a three-question quiz.

00:00:21.892 --> 00:00:26.967
Separate exchanges and contracts from individuals before measuring concentration.

00:00:26.967 --> 00:00:30.857
Accumulation/distribution is inferred, not known.

00:00:30.857 --> 00:00:33.887
"Smart money" labels carry survivorship bias.

00:00:33.887 --> 00:00:38.147
Copying wallets ignores their hedges, size and private information.

00:00:39.447 --> 00:00:41.962
Let's work an example, step by step.

00:00:41.962 --> 00:00:44.587
A "smart money" wallet buys a token.

00:00:44.587 --> 00:00:46.648
You don't see its perp short elsewhere;

00:00:46.648 --> 00:00:48.442
it may be hedged and farming.

00:00:48.442 --> 00:00:51.402
Copying the visible leg makes you the unhedged one.

00:00:52.702 --> 00:00:54.162
Here's your checklist.

00:00:54.162 --> 00:00:55.697
Do it now, for real.

00:00:55.697 --> 00:01:00.572
First, Contracts/exchanges excluded from concentration figures.

00:01:00.572 --> 00:01:03.152
And finally, Wallet-following treated as a

00:01:03.152 --> 00:01:05.012
lead to research, not a signal.

00:01:06.312 --> 00:01:07.522
Question 1.

00:01:07.522 --> 00:01:09.247
Why is wallet-copying risky?

00:01:13.667 --> 00:01:15.438
The answer: You can't see the

00:01:15.438 --> 00:01:17.327
wallet's hedges, size or intent.

00:01:18.627 --> 00:01:19.872
Question 2.

00:01:19.872 --> 00:01:21.987
What is survivorship bias in labels?

00:01:26.407 --> 00:01:28.132
The answer: Only wallets that

00:01:28.132 --> 00:01:29.857
did well get labelled "smart".

00:01:31.157 --> 00:01:32.427
Question 3.

00:01:32.427 --> 00:01:34.862
First step in measuring holder concentration?

00:01:39.282 --> 00:01:42.461
The answer: Remove exchange and contract addresses.

00:01:43.761 --> 00:01:46.276
Do the checklist now, before you move on.

00:01:46.276 --> 00:01:50.265
Next up, Lesson 7.5: Holder & supply metrics.
